hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1099","Chapter on wearing armour, 1138 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid - if Allah wills - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore two coats of mail on the day of Uhud."
"1100","1139 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not for a prophet, once he has put on his armour, to lay it down until he fights."
